{"id":"mahabharata-12-292","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":292,"title":"द्विनवत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 292 · The deluded soul and its births","summary":{"en":"Vasishtha says that by not waking to the truth, the soul passes through thousands of bodies, and describes the different austerities men practise, such as living on air, water and cow-dung. He says that the unwise man takes the unborn for born, the fearless for the fearful, and the imperishable for the perishable.","kn":"ಸತ್ಯ ಎಚ್ಚರವಾಗದ ಕಾರಣ ಆತ್ಮ ಸಾವಿರಾರು ದೇಹಗಳನ್ನು ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತದೆಂದು ವಸಿಷ್ಠ ಹೇಳಿ ಗಾಳಿ, ನೀರು, ಸಗಣಿ ಸೇವಿಸಿ ಬದುಕುವ ಮುಂತಾದ ಮನುಷ್ಯರ ತಪಸ್ಸುಗಳನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅಜ್ಞಾನಿ ಅಜನ್ಮನನ್ನು ಜನ್ಮವುಳ್ಳವನೆಂದು, ಅಭಯನನ್ನು ಭಯವುಳ್ಳವನೆಂದು, ಅಕ್ಷರನನ್ನು ಕ್ಷರನೆಂದು ತಿಳಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"वसिष्ठ कहते हैं कि सत्य के प्रति न जागने से जीव हजारों देहों में जाता है, और वायु, जल, गोबर पर जीने जैसे मनुष्यों के अनेक तप बताते हैं। वे कहते हैं कि अज्ञानी अजन्मे को जन्मा, निर्भय को भयभीत और अक्षर को क्षर मान लेता है।","te":"సత్యానికి మేల్కొనకపోవడంతో జీవుడు వేల దేహాలలోకి వెళ్తాడని వసిష్ఠుడు చెప్పి, గాలి, నీరు, ఆవు పేడతో జీవించడం వంటి మనుషుల తపస్సులను వర్ణిస్తాడు. అజ్ఞాని పుట్టనివాణ్ని పుట్టినవాడిగా, నిర్భయుని భయపడేవాడిగా, అక్షరుణ్ని క్షరుడిగా భావిస్తాడు.","ta":"உண்மைக்கு விழிக்காததால் ஆன்மா ஆயிரக்கணக்கான உடல்களில் செல்கிறது என்று வசிஷ்டர் கூறி, காற்று, நீர், சாணம் உண்டு வாழ்வது போன்ற மனிதர்களின் தவங்களை விவரிக்கிறார். அறிவிலி பிறப்பற்றவனைப் பிறந்தவனாகவும் அச்சமற்றவனை அஞ்சுபவனாகவும் அழியாததை அழிவதாகவும் எண்ணுகிறான்.","ml":"സത്യത്തിൽ ഉണരാത്തതിനാൽ ആത്മാവ് ആയിരക്കണക്കിന് ശരീരങ്ങളിലൂടെ കടന്നുപോകുന്നുവെന്ന് വസിഷ്ഠൻ പറയുന്നു; വായു, വെള്ളം, ചാണകം എന്നിവ മാത്രം കഴിച്ച് മനുഷ്യർ അനുഷ്ഠിക്കുന്ന വ്യത്യസ്ത തപസ്സുകളെയും അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു. ജന്മമില്ലാത്തതിനെ ജനിച്ചതെന്നും, ഭയമില്ലാത്തതിനെ ഭയമുള്ളതെന്നും, നശിക്കാത്തതിനെ നശിക്കുന്നതെന്നും അജ്ഞൻ കാണുന്നുവെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.292; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"वसिष्ठ उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasishtha said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमप्रतिबुद्धत्वादबुद्धमनुवर्तते ।\nदेहाद्देहसहस्राणि तथा समभिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, through lack of awakening, he follows the unawakened, and passes from body to body, thousands of bodies."}},{"n":2,"text":"तिर्यग्योनिसहस्रेषु कदाचिद्देवतास्वपि ।\nउपपद्यति संयोगाद्गुणैः सह गुणक्षयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through union with the qualities, and as the qualities are worn down, he is born among thousands of animal wombs, and sometimes among the gods."}},{"n":3,"text":"मानुषत्वाद्दिवं याति दिवो मानुष्यमेव च ।\nमानुष्यान्निरयस्थानमानन्त्यं प्रतिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"From humanhood he goes to heaven, and from heaven to humanhood again, and from humanhood he reaches the endless dwelling of hell."}},{"n":4,"text":"कोशकारो यथात्मानं कीटः समनुरुन्धति ।\nसूत्रतन्तुगुणैर्नित्यं तथायमगुणो गुणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a silkworm shuts itself in with the threads it spins, so this quality-less one, always, with the qualities."}},{"n":5,"text":"द्वंद्वमेति च निर्द्वंद्वस्तासु तास्विह योनिषु ।\nशीर्षरोगेऽक्षिरोगे च दन्तशूले गलग्रहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though free of opposites, he meets the pairs of opposites in those various wombs: disease of the head, of the eyes, toothache, a seizure of the throat,"}},{"n":6,"text":"जलोदरेऽर्शसां रोगे ज्वरगण्डविषूचिके ।\nश्वित्रे कुष्ठेऽग्निदाहे च सिध्मापस्मारयोरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"dropsy, piles, fever, boils, cholera, white leprosy, leprosy, burning with fire, skin disease and epilepsy,"}},{"n":7,"text":"यानि चान्यानि द्वंद्वानि प्राकृतानि शरीरिषु ।\nउत्पद्यन्ते विचित्राणि तान्येषोऽप्यभिमन्यते ।\nअभिमन्यत्यभीमानात्तथैव सुकृतान्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"and whatever other natural opposites arise in embodied beings, varied as they are, he takes all those as his own, and thinks the same of good deeds, through his sense of \"I.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"एकवासाश्च दुर्वासाः शायी नित्यमधस्तथा ।\nमण्डूकशायी च तथा वीरासनगतस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"One-clothed or ill-clad, always sleeping on the ground, sleeping like a frog, seated in the hero posture,"}},{"n":9,"text":"चीरधारणमाकाशे शयनं स्थानमेव च ।\nइष्टकाप्रस्तरे चैव कण्टकप्रस्तरे तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"wearing bark garments, sleeping and standing in the open air, on a bed of bricks or a bed of thorns,"}},{"n":10,"text":"भस्मप्रस्तरशायी च भूमिशय्यानुलेपनः ।\nवीरस्थानाम्बुपङ्के च शयनं फलकेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"sleeping on a bed of ashes, lying on the ground and smeared with ointment, sleeping in the hero's place, in water or mud, or on planks,"}},{"n":11,"text":"विविधासु च शय्यासु फलगृद्ध्यान्वितोऽफलः ।\nमुञ्जमेखलनग्नत्वं क्षौमकृष्णाजिनानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"on various beds, longing for fruit though without fruit, wearing a munja-grass girdle or nakedness, linen or black antelope skin,"}},{"n":12,"text":"शाणीवालपरीधानो व्याघ्रचर्मपरिच्छदः ।\nसिंहचर्मपरीधानः पट्टवासास्तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"wearing hemp or hair cloth, with a covering of tiger skin, a lion-skin garment or silk clothing,"}},{"n":13,"text":"कीटकावसनश्चैव चीरवासास्तथैव च ।\nवस्त्राणि चान्यानि बहून्यभिमन्यत्यबुद्धिमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"a covering of cocoon silk or bark; the unwise one imagines many other garments as his own,"}},{"n":14,"text":"भोजनानि विचित्राणि रत्नानि विविधानि च ।\nएकवस्त्रान्तराशित्वमेककालिकभोजनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"varied foods and various gems, eating from one cloth's width, eating once a day,"}},{"n":15,"text":"चतुर्थाष्टमकालश्च षष्ठकालिक एव च ।\nषड्रात्रभोजनश्चैव तथैवाष्टाहभोजनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"eating on the fourth or eighth or sixth time, eating every six nights or every eight days,"}},{"n":16,"text":"सप्तरात्रदशाहारो द्वादशाहार एव च ।\nमासोपवासी मूलाशी फलाहारस्तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"eating after seven nights, ten days or twelve days, fasting for a month, living on roots and fruits,"}},{"n":17,"text":"वायुभक्षोऽम्बुपिण्याकगोमयादन एव च ।\nगोमूत्रभोजनश्चैव शाकपुष्पाद एव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"living on air, water, oil-cake and cow dung, living on cow urine, vegetables and flowers,"}},{"n":18,"text":"शैवालभोजनश्चैव तथाचामेन वर्तयन् ।\nवर्तयञ्शीर्णपर्णैश्च प्रकीर्णफलभोजनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"living on water-moss and on rice-scum alone, living on fallen leaves and scattered fruit,"}},{"n":19,"text":"विविधानि च कृच्छ्राणि सेवते सुखकाङ्क्षया ।\nचान्द्रायणानि विधिवल्लिङ्गानि विविधानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"and practicing many penances out of the wish for happiness, the Chandrayana vows by rule and various outward marks."}},{"n":20,"text":"चातुराश्रम्यपन्थानमाश्रयत्याश्रमानपि ।\nउपासीनश्च पाषण्डान्गुहाः शैलांस्तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"He takes to the path of the four orders of life and its stages; he attends heretics, caves and mountains,"}},{"n":21,"text":"विविक्ताश्च शिलाछायास्तथा प्रस्रवणानि च ।\nविविधानि च जप्यानि विविधानि व्रतानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"solitary places, shade of rocks and springs, various recitations, various vows,"}},{"n":22,"text":"नियमान्सुविचित्रांश्च विविधानि तपांसि च ।\nयज्ञांश्च विविधाकारान्विधींश्च विविधांस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"various rules, very varied austerities, and sacrifices of many kinds and many rites,"}},{"n":23,"text":"वणिक्पथं द्विजक्षत्रं वैश्यशूद्रं तथैव च ।\nदानं च विविधाकारं दीनान्धकृपणेष्वपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"the way of the merchant, the twice-born Kshatriya, the Vaishya and the Shudra, and gifts of many kinds, even to the wretched, the blind and the miserly."}},{"n":24,"text":"अभिमन्यत्यसंबोधात्तथैव त्रिविधान्गुणान् ।\nसत्त्वं रजस्तमश्चैव धर्मार्थौ काम एव च ।\nप्रकृत्यात्मानमेवात्मा एवं प्रविभजत्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through lack of awakening he takes the threefold qualities as his own: sattva, rajas and tamas, and dharma, wealth and desire; so the self divides itself by nature."}},{"n":25,"text":"स्वधाकारवषट्कारौ स्वाहाकारनमस्क्रियाः ।\nयाजनाध्यापनं दानं तथैवाहुः प्रतिग्रहम् ।\nयजनाध्ययने चैव यच्चान्यदपि किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Svadha and vashat, svaha and homage, officiating, teaching, giving and likewise accepting gifts, sacrificing and studying, and anything else of the sort,"}},{"n":26,"text":"जन्ममृत्युविवादे च तथा विशसनेऽपि च ।\nशुभाशुभमयं सर्वमेतदाहुः क्रियापथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"in birth and death and quarrel, and also in slaughter: all this, made of good and bad, they call the path of action."}},{"n":27,"text":"प्रकृतिः कुरुते देवी महाप्रलयमेव च ।\nदिवसान्ते गुणानेतानभ्येत्यैकोऽवतिष्ठति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The goddess Nature brings about even the great dissolution; at the end of the day, approaching these qualities, one alone remains."}},{"n":28,"text":"रश्मिजालमिवादित्यस्तत्कालेन नियच्छति ।\nएवमेषोऽसकृत्सर्वं क्रीडार्थमभिमन्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the sun draws in its net of rays, so at that time he holds them back. So, repeatedly, he takes everything as his own for sport."}},{"n":29,"text":"आत्मरूपगुणानेतान्विविधान्हृदयप्रियान् ।\nएवमेव विकुर्वाणः सर्गप्रलयकर्मणी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus transforming these various qualities dear to his heart, which belong to the form of the self, he does the work of creation and dissolution."}},{"n":30,"text":"क्रियाक्रियापथे रक्तस्त्रिगुणस्त्रिगुणातिगः ।\nक्रियाक्रियापथोपेतस्तथा तदिति मन्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Attached to the path of action and inaction, three-qualitied and yet beyond the three qualities, joined to the path of action and inaction, he thinks it to be so."}},{"n":31,"text":"एवं द्वंद्वान्यथैतानि वर्तन्ते मम नित्यशः ।\nममैवैतानि जायन्ते बाधन्ते तानि मामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"These opposites always occur to me; these arise in me; these torment me.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"निस्तर्तव्यान्यथैतानि सर्वाणीति नराधिप ।\nमन्यतेऽयं ह्यबुद्धित्वात्तथैव सुकृतान्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"He thinks, king, \"All these must be got through,\" through lack of awakening, and likewise his good deeds."}},{"n":33,"text":"भोक्तव्यानि मयैतानि देवलोकगतेन वै ।\nइहैव चैनं भोक्ष्यामि शुभाशुभफलोदयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"These I shall enjoy when I have gone to the world of the gods; here itself I shall enjoy the arising of fruit, good and bad.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"सुखमेव च कर्तव्यं सकृत्कृत्वा सुखं मम ।\nयावदन्तं च मे सौख्यं जात्यां जात्यां भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Happiness must be made; having once made it, happiness will be mine, and my happiness will last to the end in birth after birth.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"भविष्यति च मे दुःखं कृतेनेहाप्यनन्तकम् ।\nमहद्दुःखं हि मानुष्यं निरये चापि मज्जनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And by what I have done here, endless suffering will be mine as well; human life is great suffering, and so is sinking in hell.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"निरयाच्चापि मानुष्यं कालेनैष्याम्यहं पुनः ।\nमनुष्यत्वाच्च देवत्वं देवत्वात्पौरुषं पुनः ।\nमनुष्यत्वाच्च निरयं पर्यायेणोपगच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And from hell I shall come to the human state again in time; from humanhood to godhood, from godhood to manhood again, and from humanhood he goes by turns to hell.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"य एवं वेत्ति वै नित्यं निरात्मात्मगुणैर्वृतः ।\nतेन देवमनुष्येषु निरये चोपपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who always knows it thus, without a self, wrapped in the qualities of the self, is reborn among gods and men and in hell."}},{"n":38,"text":"ममत्वेनावृतो नित्यं तत्रैव परिवर्तते ।\nसर्गकोटिसहस्राणि मरणान्तासु मूर्तिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Always wrapped in the sense of \"mine,\" he turns round in that same place, through thousands of crores of creations, in forms ending in death."}},{"n":39,"text":"य एवं कुरुते कर्म शुभाशुभफलात्मकम् ।\nस एव फलमश्नाति त्रिषु लोकेषु मूर्तिमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who does the action whose fruit is good and bad is himself the one embodied who eats the fruit in the three worlds."}},{"n":40,"text":"प्रकृतिः कुरुते कर्म शुभाशुभफलात्मकम् ।\nप्रकृतिश्च तदश्नाति त्रिषु लोकेषु कामगा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nature does the action whose fruit is good and bad, and Nature eats it, moving at will in the three worlds."}},{"n":41,"text":"तिर्यग्योनौ मनुष्यत्वे देवलोके तथैव च ।\nत्रीणि स्थानानि चैतानि जानीयात्प्राकृतानि ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know these three as the states belonging to Nature: the animal womb, humanhood, and the world of the gods."}},{"n":42,"text":"अलिङ्गां प्रकृतिं त्वाहुर्लिङ्गैरनुमिमीमहे ।\nतथैव पौरुषं लिङ्गमनुमानाद्धि पश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"They call Nature without mark, yet we infer it from marks; in the same way the spirit sees its own mark by inference."}},{"n":43,"text":"स लिङ्गान्तरमासाद्य प्राकृतं लिङ्गमव्रणम् ।\nव्रणद्वाराण्यधिष्ठाय कर्माण्यात्मनि मन्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having reached another mark, the unwounded mark born of Nature, he occupies the doors of the wound and thinks that actions belong to the self."}},{"n":44,"text":"श्रोत्रादीनि तु सर्वाणि पञ्च कर्मेन्द्रियाणि च ।\nवागादीनि प्रवर्तन्ते गुणेष्वेव गुणैः सह ।\nअहमेतानि वै कुर्वन्ममैतानीन्द्रियाणि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ear and the rest, and the five organs of action beginning with speech, work among the qualities only, with the qualities. \"I do these, and these senses are mine,\" he thinks."}},{"n":45,"text":"निरिन्द्रियोऽभिमन्येत व्रणवानस्मि निर्व्रणः ।\nअलिङ्गो लिङ्गमात्मानमकालः कालमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though without senses, he imagines \"I am wounded\" while unwounded, markless he thinks the mark his own, timeless he thinks time his own,"}},{"n":46,"text":"असत्त्वं सत्त्वमात्मानमतत्त्वं तत्त्वमात्मनः ।\nअमृत्युर्मृत्युमात्मानमचरश्चरमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"without being he thinks being his own, without principle he thinks principle his own, deathless he thinks death his own, unmoving he thinks the moving his own,"}},{"n":47,"text":"अक्षेत्रः क्षेत्रमात्मानमसर्गः सर्गमात्मनः ।\nअतपास्तप आत्मानमगतिर्गतिमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"fieldless he thinks the field his own, without creation he thinks creation his own, without austerity he thinks austerity his own, without a course he thinks a course his own,"}},{"n":48,"text":"अभवो भवमात्मानमभयो भयमात्मनः ।\nअक्षरः क्षरमात्मानमबुद्धिस्त्वभिमन्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"without becoming he thinks becoming his own, fearless he thinks fear his own, imperishable he thinks the perishable his own; so the unawakened one imagines."}}]}]}